{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>At that time HaShem set apart the tribe of Levi</b> — this refers back to the earlier matter: \"at that time,\" in the first year when you came out of Egypt and sinned with the calf, while the sons of Levi did not sin — the Place set them apart from you. This is the language of Rashi (Rashi on Deuteronomy 10:8). If so, he says that from that time they were set apart before Him, may He be blessed, for He did not actually separate them in deed until the second year, in the second month. Or he may allude to what He said to them (Exodus 32:29), \"Fill your hands today to HaShem\" — for this would constitute their consecration for the service of priesthood and Leviteship. But the correct interpretation in my eyes is that <b>at that time</b> means the second time, just like the first (Deuteronomy 10:1), for at the time He said to him, \"Hew for yourself two tablets of stone\" (Exodus 34:1), He was reconciled to Israel and commanded concerning the Tabernacle, and then He was also reconciled to Aaron and commanded (Exodus 28:4), \"And they shall make holy garments for Aaron your brother and his sons, to sanctify him to minister to Me,\" and commanded him concerning the consecration service. Therefore he says that Elazar served as priest in his father's stead, for the anointing of priesthood for all their generations was upon them. And He made the separation of the entire tribe one matter, for from that day it was before Him that his tribe would be given over to Him to perform the service of the Tabernacle. Or he may say that the tribe of Levi was set apart at that time so that the priests would come from among them, for they too bear the Ark, as it says, \"And he gave it to the priests, the sons of Levi, who bear the Ark of the covenant of HaShem\" (Deuteronomy 31:9), and they are the ones who minister to HaShem and bless in His name. And the reason for \"until this day\" is on account of the priesthood of Elazar, meaning: then He set them apart to minister to Him, and so it has been until this day."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T02:47:34.624071634Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}